4no|n|To stop; to check or hinder the motion or action of; as, to arrest the current of a river; to arrest the senses. ; To take, seize, or apprehend by authority of law; as, to arrest one for debt, or for a crime. ; To seize on and fix; to hold; to catch; as, to arrest the eyes or attention. ; To rest or fasten; to fix; to concentrate. ; To tarry; to rest. ; The act of stopping, or restraining from further motion, etc.; stoppage; hindrance; restraint; as, an arrest of development. ; The taking or apprehending of a person by authority of law; legal restraint; custody. Also, a decree, mandate, or warrant. ; Any seizure by power, physical or moral. ; A scurfiness of the back part of the hind leg of a horse; -- also named rat-tails.	a:as4,117,14~as4,117,14	v:as4,79,1~as4,79,1	n:as4,79,1;ykq,76,4;hfg,58,5;251z,22,3~hfg,58,5;ykq,76,4;251z,22,3;as4,79,1
